300" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161843/selection/a35fa3f1e567966a4d0c9564617d9c5635161e731ebf5a9a4f641eb4ed687c67" :answer-field/choices ["q-161843/selection/e68d68c408167483851bd23bd07eeea3a8a4a586e50cb182d440fd7888c8913b" "q-161843/selection/7fac53ea6869232c6155db40596d0d058af7a5c5d4a99c1e59b0a45a6e687b58" "q-161843/selection/a35fa3f1e567966a4d0c9564617d9c5635161e731ebf5a9a4f641eb4ed687c67" "q-161843/selection/57b7c34c3d012cd8f978d39e4aaeb57c1a1533ec0f1a3f157bdd0b2ed9f83c6f" "q-161843/selection/8e29a31b3c0564ac5398e6731ea26a74b8606d51b809b7f6d443725918adeb40"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161843" :question/id #uuid "4a1b487f-874e-5662-8cb4-0ff2c90e3298" :question/math-academy-id "q-161843" :question/problem "Which of the following shows the region in the $uv$-plane where the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}4u+{v}^{2} \\\\ v-{u}^{2}\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nis (locally) orientation-preserving?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a transformation is (locally) orientation-preserving at the points where the Jacobian determinant is positive:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}>0.\n$$\n\nWe have\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}4u+{v}^{2} \\\\ v-{u}^{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2v \\\\ -2u & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4\\cdot 1-(-2u)\\cdot (2v) \\\\  & =4+4uv.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the required regions, we solve the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4+4uv & >0 \\\\ 4uv & >-4 \\\\ uv & >-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThis gives the solution $v>-\\frac{1}{u}$ for $u>0$ and $v<-\\frac{1}{u}$ for $u<0.$\n\nNotice that the equation \n\n$$\nv=-\\frac{1}{u}\n$$\n\ndefines a hyperbola, and the coordinates of, say, $(1,1)$ and $(-1,-1)$ satisfy the inequality. \n\nTherefore, the region where the transformation is (locally) orientation-preserving must be the following:\n\n  \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066185/assets/c501e7e341af57e86f18d73871314800d453f79572e16ccf2477335352d4dcdc.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-161843/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "091b8235-56d8-5a08-bc95-08c99772cfd8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161843"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-161856/selection/57b7c34c3d012cd8f978d39e4aaeb57c1a1533ec0f1a3f157bdd0b2ed9f83c6f" :answer/id #uuid "e2710562-98ac-5e9b-bb7e-966ec4f09f49" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066185/assets/c244350524a52123e2e97db4cd8eb4f57737b8b15746eb72a8d54eac32a4f3cf.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161856/selection/7fac53ea6869232c6155db40596d0d058af7a5c5d4a99c1e59b0a45a6e687b58" :answer/id #uuid "fd1def52-dd46-56d3-9c0f-d25733d66390" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066185/assets/d477a9f312fc2fb0a5a4c2d13164c96118aa70b53cf23db80be9ec698151e6fd.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161856/selection/8525b92d40e3fb8aae1298dac7d1f62df6606be3a9632e7e5326dd1958dc339f" :answer/id #uuid "3c7311c2-b4c7-5f25-887d-9d8a7656ca4d" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066185/assets/fe7bb422a3f992ea88a900e63b2c55df99bce3a785929901c248abadfadf23f1.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161856/selection/53bb708e6743bf962d9d3d140e69e70